WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:16.309
Fire And Blood will reign again and you can
expect to see the Blackfyre Rebellions in

00:00:16.309 --> 00:00:21.060
the later seasons of House of the Dragon!
That includes one of the most prominent and

00:00:21.060 --> 00:00:25.470
key figures from this time period,
Brynden ''Bloodraven'' Rivers who was the

00:00:25.470 --> 00:00:30.890
main Targaryen general fighting against Blackfyres.
The same man who would later go on to become

00:00:30.890 --> 00:00:34.449
the three-eyed raven and teach Bran Stark
his abilities.

00:00:34.449 --> 00:00:38.930
The upcoming Game of Thrones prequel series,
House of the Dragon, is based on George RR

00:00:38.930 --> 00:00:43.800
Martin's Targaryen history book Fire &amp; Blood.
House of the Dragon is a Game of Thrones prequel

00:00:43.800 --> 00:00:47.579
show that is confirmed by HBO’s president
to air in 2022.

00:00:47.579 --> 00:00:53.489
Miguel Sapochnik and Ryan Condal will serve
as showrunners and executive producers. George

00:00:53.489 --> 00:00:56.130
R. R. Martin will also serve as executive
producer.

00:00:56.130 --> 00:01:02.660
It is based on George RR Martin’s book Fire
And Blood volume 1 and on Martin’s yet unfinished

00:01:02.660 --> 00:01:06.200
Fire And Blood volume 2 book.
“Fire &amp; Blood begins their tale with the

00:01:06.200 --> 00:01:11.070
legendary Aegon the Conqueror, creator of
the Iron Throne, and goes on to recount the

00:01:11.070 --> 00:01:15.820
generations of Targaryens who fought to hold
that iconic seat, all the way up to the civil

00:01:15.820 --> 00:01:20.700
war that nearly tore their dynasty apart.”
In other words it covers events from Aegon's

00:01:20.700 --> 00:01:25.090
Conquest to the Dance of the Dragons.
That's Fire And Blood volume 1.

00:01:25.090 --> 00:01:29.390
House of the Dragon will start with a build
up towards the Dance of the Dragons and early

00:01:29.390 --> 00:01:34.550
seasons will cover the Dance itself. Later
seasons however, will be based on George RR

00:01:34.550 --> 00:01:37.700
Martin’s yet unfinished Fire And Blood volume
2 book .

00:01:37.700 --> 00:01:43.170
The yet unreleased Fire And Blood volume 2
will continue from where part 1 ended, with

00:01:43.170 --> 00:01:48.690
Rhaenyra Targaryen's son Aegon lll's reign
and will cover Blackyre rebellions, war with

00:01:48.690 --> 00:01:54.310
Dorne and go all the way to the Mad King and
Robert's Rebellion that ended Targaryen dynasty.

00:01:54.310 --> 00:01:58.571
As I already said, one of the most important
characters from this time period of the Blackfyre

00:01:58.571 --> 00:02:03.170
Rebellions was Ser Brynden Rivers, called
"Lord Bloodraven".

00:02:03.170 --> 00:02:09.569
He was the bastard son of King Aegon IV Targaryen
by his sixth mistress, Lady Melissa Blackwood.

00:02:09.569 --> 00:02:16.660
He had two older sisters and numerous half-siblings.
As his mother was highborn, Brynden was counted

00:02:16.660 --> 00:02:21.680
among the Great Bastards.
Like his bastard siblings, Brynden was legitimized

00:02:21.680 --> 00:02:28.189
by King Aegon IV in 184 AC.
Brynden's personal arms were a white dragon

00:02:28.189 --> 00:02:32.120
with red eyes breathing red flame on a black
field.

00:02:32.120 --> 00:02:38.040
Brynden was an albino and thus had milky-white
skin, long white hair, and red eyes.

00:02:38.040 --> 00:02:42.870
On the right side of his face he had a red
wine stain birthmark that extended from his

00:02:42.870 --> 00:02:47.489
throat up to his right cheek from which he
earned his name Bloodraven,

00:02:47.489 --> 00:02:52.079
as the birthmark was said to look somewhat
like a raven drawn in blood.

00:02:52.079 --> 00:02:57.230
Brynden was not as tall or muscular as his
half brothers, Daemon Blackfyre and Aegor

00:02:57.230 --> 00:03:01.019
Bittersteel,
but he was considered more cunning. Brynden

00:03:01.019 --> 00:03:04.079
carried the Valyrian steel longsword Dark
Sister

00:03:04.079 --> 00:03:09.540
and was a good swordsman, he was an expert
bowman who preferred to use his tall weirwood

00:03:09.540 --> 00:03:13.260
longbow.
Brynden was rumored to be a sinister sorcerer

00:03:13.260 --> 00:03:19.719
and spymaster who effectively ruled the kingdom
"with spies and spells" and as "Lord Bloodraven".

00:03:19.719 --> 00:03:24.610
A popular riddle asked was,
"How many eyes does Lord Bloodraven have?

00:03:24.610 --> 00:03:28.629
A thousand eyes, and one".
The song "A Thousand Eyes, and One" was written

00:03:28.629 --> 00:03:32.590
about Brynden.
Brynden was resented by his half brother Aegor

00:03:32.590 --> 00:03:37.859
Rivers, nicknamed "Bittersteel".
At some point, Brynden became a lover to his

00:03:37.859 --> 00:03:43.420
half-sister, Shiera Seastar.
As Aegor desired her as well, Shiera became

00:03:43.420 --> 00:03:49.769
another point of rivalry between the two half-siblings.
Bittersteel became a great champion and general

00:03:49.769 --> 00:03:54.799
for his half brother Daemon Blackfyre,
while Bloodraven became a great champion and

00:03:54.799 --> 00:04:01.640
general for his half brother Daeron II Targaryen.
The First Blackfyre Rebellion ended in 196

00:04:01.640 --> 00:04:06.739
AC with the Battle of Redgrass Field,
in which Daemon Blackfyre and his eldest two

00:04:06.739 --> 00:04:11.269
sons were slain.
It was Bloodraven's private company of archers,

00:04:11.269 --> 00:04:15.950
known as the Raven's Teeth,
who rained arrows down upon Daemon Blackfyre

00:04:15.950 --> 00:04:21.680
and his two eldest sons, killing them.
Many called Bloodraven a kingslayer for this,

00:04:21.680 --> 00:04:27.150
although no one knew exactly whose arrows
had killed Daemon - he was pierced by many.

00:04:27.150 --> 00:04:31.290
The arrows are said to have been driven by
Brynden's sorcery.

00:04:31.290 --> 00:04:37.230
Daemon's death led the rebels to rout, but
some were rallied by Aegor Rivers in mad charge.

00:04:37.230 --> 00:04:42.420
The resulting duel between the rival half
brothers left Brynden blinded in one eye and

00:04:42.420 --> 00:04:46.970
Aegor retreating.
The battle was lost, but Bittersteel managed

00:04:46.970 --> 00:04:51.850
to escape, and became one of the major leaders
of the surviving Blackfyre forces as they

00:04:51.850 --> 00:04:56.770
fled into exile in the Free Cities.
Daemon left behind five sons and multiple

00:04:56.770 --> 00:05:02.640
daughters, so Bittersteel became their guardian.
They would continue to harass the Seven Kingdoms

00:05:02.640 --> 00:05:08.290
with plots and failed rebellions for decades.
After King Daeron II died in the Great Spring

00:05:08.290 --> 00:05:15.720
Sickness of 209 AC he was succeeded by his
son Aerys I Targaryen - who proved to be weak,

00:05:15.720 --> 00:05:21.480
absentee-king, more concerned with introverted
scholarly pursuits than any form of governing.

00:05:21.480 --> 00:05:27.380
When Aerys I was crowned, however, Bloodraven
was named as the new Hand of the King, a position

00:05:27.380 --> 00:05:33.310
he held throughout Aerys I's twelve-year reign.
During that time, Bloodraven was the real

00:05:33.310 --> 00:05:38.891
power behind the throne, and the functional
ruler of the Seven Kingdoms. Aerys I's rule

00:05:38.891 --> 00:05:42.990
was deeply troubled by plague, drought, and
insurrection,

00:05:42.990 --> 00:05:45.990
and many blamed Bloodraven because he was
in charge,

00:05:45.990 --> 00:05:48.790
but ultimately he was the man holding the
realm

00:05:48.790 --> 00:05:52.730
back from the brink of chaos during this troubled
period.

00:05:52.730 --> 00:05:57.650
During his time as Hand of the King, Brynden
was not only an effective administrator and

00:05:57.650 --> 00:06:01.410
strategist,
but a cunning spy-master, and the information

00:06:01.410 --> 00:06:07.450
from his secret agents greatly aided his grip
on power. His spies were so widespread that,

00:06:07.450 --> 00:06:12.621
also referring to the eye he lost in battle,
a popular riddle at the time asked, "How many

00:06:12.621 --> 00:06:16.930
eyes does Lord Bloodraven have?"
to which the answer was "A thousand eyes...

00:06:16.930 --> 00:06:21.100
and one...".
Some people alleged that Brynden and his paramour,

00:06:21.100 --> 00:06:26.530
his half-sister Shiera Seastar,
used sorcery to uncover secrets. During the

00:06:26.530 --> 00:06:30.949
wedding tourney at Whitewalls in 212 AC,
and through his informants, including a man-at-arms

00:06:30.949 --> 00:06:36.830
and a troupe of comic dwarfs,
Brynden was aware of a plot at Whitewalls

00:06:36.830 --> 00:06:42.190
to put Daemon II Blackfyre forward as the
legitimate Lord of the Seven Kingdoms.

00:06:42.190 --> 00:06:46.530
Brynden marched on the tourney with three
hundred Raven's Teeth, three brothers of the

00:06:46.530 --> 00:06:52.320
Kingsguard, five hundred other knights, and
five thousand infantry drawn from the crownlands

00:06:52.320 --> 00:06:56.330
and the riverlands.
In the face of such a force Daemon tried to

00:06:56.330 --> 00:07:02.180
rally the tourney-goers to battle, but found
little support. Daemon then challenged Bloodraven

00:07:02.180 --> 00:07:07.900
to single combat; Brynden refused and arrested
the pretender, thus containing the Second

00:07:07.900 --> 00:07:12.560
Blackfyre Rebellion.
Daemon was kept in captivity rather than executed

00:07:12.560 --> 00:07:17.150
with the other rebel leaders,
ensuring that Aegor Rivers could not name

00:07:17.150 --> 00:07:22.340
his brother Haegon as a serious pretender.
However, Daemon died few years later while

00:07:22.340 --> 00:07:26.810
a hostage in the Red Keep,
and Haegon and Bittersteel launched the Third

00:07:26.810 --> 00:07:30.600
Blackfyre Rebellion.
The Third Blackfyre Rebellion featured the

00:07:30.600 --> 00:07:34.940
second duel between Brynden
and his half brother Bittersteel. At the end

00:07:34.940 --> 00:07:40.390
of the final battle, the Pretender Haegon
was dishonorably killed after he had surrendered

00:07:40.390 --> 00:07:44.760
and had given up his sword. Bittersteel was
taken captive.

00:07:44.760 --> 00:07:49.740
In the aftermath of the Third Blackfyre Rebellion,
Brynden argued that the captive Aegor Rivers

00:07:49.740 --> 00:07:55.560
should be put to death, but King Aerys I Targaryen
decided to send Aegor to the Night's Watch

00:07:55.560 --> 00:08:00.900
instead. However, Aegor Rivers escaped back
to Essos when his ship was intercepted en

00:08:00.900 --> 00:08:05.480
route to Eastwatch,
thus the Blackfyre plotting continued. Brynden

00:08:05.480 --> 00:08:12.450
continued as Hand for Aerys's successor,
his brother Maekar I, in 221 AC. After Maekar's

00:08:12.450 --> 00:08:16.040
death in 233 AC, Brynden, as the Hand of the
King,

00:08:16.040 --> 00:08:21.010
called a Great Council in King's Landing to
discuss disputed matter of succession.

00:08:21.010 --> 00:08:27.200
Aerys I died in 221 AC without issue, so he
was succeeded by his younger brother Maekar

00:08:27.200 --> 00:08:32.969
Targaryen. Even though Maekar distrusted his
uncle, he kept Bloodraven as Hand of the King.

00:08:32.969 --> 00:08:39.789
Maekar ruled for twelve years and was then
succeeded by his own son, Aegon V Targaryen,

00:08:39.789 --> 00:08:44.810
also known as "Egg". During the Great Council
that put Aegon V on the throne,

00:08:44.810 --> 00:08:50.399
Aenys Blackfyre had sent word from the Free
Cities that he wanted to put himself forth

00:08:50.399 --> 00:08:56.449
as a legitimate candidate. Bloodraven promised
him safe passage and Aenys accepted in good

00:08:56.449 --> 00:08:59.839
faith,
but as soon as he set foot in King's Landing,

00:08:59.839 --> 00:09:04.370
the Gold Cloaks seized him
and dragged him to the Red Keep, where Bloodraven

00:09:04.370 --> 00:09:09.149
promptly executed him.
This was decried as utterly dishonorable,

00:09:09.149 --> 00:09:13.720
but Bloodraven said he willingly paid the
price to remove one more potential Blackfyre

00:09:13.720 --> 00:09:17.329
pretender, and accepted exile to the Night's
Watch as punishment.

00:09:17.329 --> 00:09:23.730
In 233 AC, the year he was crowned, Aegon
V had Bloodraven sent north

00:09:23.730 --> 00:09:30.190
as part of the "honor guard" that escorted
his older brother, Maester Aemon, to the Wall.

00:09:30.190 --> 00:09:34.759
Brynden took Dark Sister with him when he
went to the Wall. In time, Bloodraven rose

00:09:34.759 --> 00:09:39.410
to become the new Lord Commander. He served
long and well in this position,

00:09:39.410 --> 00:09:45.350
but one day he went out alone ranging beyond
the Wall, and mysteriously never returned.

00:09:45.350 --> 00:09:50.310
Around 50 years later Bran Stark discovers
that Brynden is still alive as the three-eyed

00:09:50.310 --> 00:09:53.779
crow,
the last greenseer living with children of

00:09:53.779 --> 00:09:58.009
the forest in a cave beyond the Wall.
In George RR Martin's books, the three-eyed

00:09:58.009 --> 00:10:02.410
raven reveals the following:
''I wore many names when I was quick, but

00:10:02.410 --> 00:10:06.199
even I had a mother,
and the name she gave me at her breast was

00:10:06.199 --> 00:10:11.439
Brynden.'' He also tells Bran this:
''I have my own ghosts, Bran. A brother that

00:10:11.439 --> 00:10:16.110
I loved (which would be Daeron),
a brother that I hated (which would be Bittersteel),

00:10:16.110 --> 00:10:21.410
a woman I desired (which would be Shiera).''
The three-eyed raven also said to Bran the

00:10:21.410 --> 00:10:24.340
following:
''I have been watching you. All of you. All

00:10:24.340 --> 00:10:28.970
of your lives, with a thousand eyes and one.''
We know that a popular riddle asked about

00:10:28.970 --> 00:10:32.970
Brynden in his youth was,
"How many eyes does Lord Bloodraven have?

00:10:32.970 --> 00:10:36.639
A thousand eyes, and one".
The song "A Thousand Eyes, and One" was written

00:10:36.639 --> 00:10:40.199
about Brynden,
so that's a nice little final confirmation

00:10:40.199 --> 00:10:43.990
of Lord Bloodraven that he indeed became the
three-eyed raven.

00:10:43.990 --> 00:10:48.121
That's the story of the main Targaryen loyalist
fighting against the Blackfyres in the Blackfyre

00:10:48.121 --> 00:10:54.389
rebellions, Brynden Rivers known as Lord Bloodraven.
Legendary characters such as Brynden himself

00:10:54.389 --> 00:10:58.779
as well as Daemon Blackfyre and Bittersteel
as well as dozens of characters coming before

00:10:58.779 --> 00:11:03.170
them in the Dance of the Dragons,
legendary battles such as the Battle of Redgrass

00:11:03.170 --> 00:11:08.050
Field and many other coming before and after,
all of that and more this Game of Thrones

00:11:08.050 --> 00:11:11.800
prequel show, House of the Dragon, brings
in 2022,

00:11:11.800 --> 00:11:14.160
although the rebellions will be in the later
seasons of the show.

00:11:14.160 --> 00:11:17.300
Let me know your thoughts about all of this
in the comment section down below.

00:11:17.300 --> 00:11:19.519
Thank you so much for watching and hope to
see you in the next one.

00:11:19.519 --> 00:11:19.529
Peace!

